    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2010.01188v1</id>
    <title>On commuting probabilities in finite groups and rings</title>
    <updated>2020-10-02T20:34:22Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2010.01188v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2010.01188v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>We show that the set of all commuting probabilities in finite rings is a subset of the set of all commuting probabilities in finite nilpotent groups of class $\le2$. We believe that these two sets are equal; we prove they are equal, when restricted to groups and rings with odd number of elements.</summary>
    <category term="math.RA" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
